ddle Low German wagen."},{"parola":"ättika","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"ereditato","incerta":"no","significato":"Various concentrations of acetic acid; white vinegar.","termine_origine":"edik","catena":[{"codice":"non","nome":"Old Norse","termine":"edik","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"etik","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"dum","nome":"Middle Dutch","termine":"edik","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gmw-pro","nome":"Proto-West Germanic","termine":"*atek","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"la","nome":"Latin","termine":"acētum","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"la","ambiti":["cucina"],"via":"","testo":"From late Old Norse edik, from Middle Low German etik or Middle Dutch edik, from Proto-West Germanic *atek, metathesized variant of *aket, from Latin acētum. Compare Faroese edikur, Norwegian Bokmål eddik, Danish eddike, Icelandic edik, Old English æċed, German Essig. According to SO attested since "},{"parola":"äventyr","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"ereditato","incerta":"no","significato":"an adventure (unusual, exciting (and dangerous) undertaking or experience)","termine_origine":"æfintýr","catena":[{"codice":"non","nome":"Old Norse","termine":"æfintýr","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"eventü̂re","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"frm","nome":"Middle French","termine":"adventure","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"frm","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From late Old Norse æfintýr, from Middle Low German eventü̂r, from Middle French adventure (“aventure”)."}]}